urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.db51c25932a0ae506cdad9b4c4c5ca862782230d.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 2 at 12:37PM MDT until September 2 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWest Central Mesa County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 330 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1237 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. The expected rainfall rate is 1\nto 3 inches in 1 hour. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.2 to 0.5\ninches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing\nor expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Thunderstorms producing flash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of creeks, arroyos, and streams, streets\nand underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nGrand Junction, Fruita and Colorado National Monument.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nDevils Canyon, Monument Canyon, and Wedding Canyon","ends":"2026-09-02T15:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.663443da938e7db9d4a6c151a8a6a3856556e2e8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.663443da938e7db9d4a6c151a8a6a3856556e2e8.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued September 2 at 11:28AM MDT until September 2 at 2:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Urban areas and small streams flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Mesa County in west central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 230 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of creeks, streams, arroyos and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1126 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly\nin the warned area. Between 0.3 and 0.8 inches of rain have\nfallen. Rainfall rates of 1 to 3 inches per hour are expected\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nLayton Wash, Dry Gulch, Reed Wash, Lipan Wash, Adobe Creek,\nCoyote Wash, Big Salt Wash and Little Salt Wash.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFruita and Loma.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-02T14:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.36ab7c674d65e9c18d6ba099d79ad070c7a185dd.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.36ab7c674d65e9c18d6ba099d79ad070c7a185dd.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-02T18:05:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 021805 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1205 PM MDT Wed Sep 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Afternoon showers and thunderstorms continue today and Wednesday, with a diminishing flash flooding risk. - Gusty winds return Wednesday and Thursday, with afternoon gusts to around 35 mph for much of the region. - A chance for additional monsoonal moistur","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-02T07:55:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... A few showers and thunderstorms will be possible this afternoon as a weak wave moves through. Aloft, the jet stream will move across the area and with deeper mixing expected, some gusty winds of 30 to 40 mph will be possible this afternoon and through the end of the week. Humidities will remain above any critical fire weather thresholds so do not anticipate any critical fire weather","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"orm02","station_name":"CSU Orchard Mesa Research Station","distance_km":7.5,"soil_temp_5cm_f":72.32,"soil_temp_15cm_f":70.2,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"s